menuconfig LIBVULKAN
	bool "libvulkan: application-facing Vulkan ABI/runtime (compute-first subset)"
	default n
	select LIBUKVULKAN_VENUS
	select LIBUKVIRTIO_GPU
	select LIBUKLOCK
	select LIBUKLOCK_MUTEX
	help
	  Application-facing Vulkan ABI/runtime boundary for Unikraft. libvulkan
	  owns the exported vk* symbols, vkGetInstanceProcAddr/vkGetDeviceProcAddr,
	  the Vulkan-Hpp DispatchLoaderDynamic storage/init glue, and the common
	  Vulkan runtime state needed by the supported compute-first subset. It
	  dispatches the public Vulkan entry points to a statically linked Vulkan
	  driver implementation.

	  The current driver is the Unikraft-native Venus driver
	  (CONFIG_LIBUKVULKAN_VENUS), which libvulkan selects. The dispatch bootstrap
	  opens the VirtIO-GPU/Venus context through that driver's native
	  libukvirtio_gpu path (no Linux virtgpu DRM UAPI); libvulkan does NOT
	  own the Venus wire format, VirtIO-GPU probing, Linux DRM compatibility, or
	  any ggml/GGUF/llama runtime logic.

	  This is a compute-first Vulkan API subset (the slice required by upstream
	  ggml-vulkan.cpp); it is not full Vulkan and not Vulkan conformance. See
	  README.md for the claim boundary.

if LIBVULKAN

config LIBVULKAN_ENABLE_DRM_FD_COMPAT
	bool "Enable Linux DRM fd compatibility provider"
	default n
	select LIBUKVIRTGPU_DRM
	select LIBUKVIRTGPU_DRM_FDIO
	help
	  Opt-in compatibility path for Mesa/Linux-style Vulkan applications that
	  expect /dev/dri/renderD128, DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_* and mmap(fd, offset).
	  Native VOGUE Vulkan/llama builds must leave this disabled; the default
	  libvulkan path dispatches through libukvulkan_venus directly over
	  libukvirtio_gpu and does not need Linux DRM UAPI state.

endif
